link { url = "https://github.com/kalandra-lang/kalandra/blob/native/docs/design/numbers.md", "Numeric rules and conversion details" }


h2 { "Arithmetic execution policy" }

CPU float32 and float64 arithmetic use hardware floating-point instructions by default. Floating comparisons and checked conversions also use hardware where supported. Integer overflow and conversion range checks remain enabled.

Use --arithmetic software to select the strict integer-based floating implementation. Hardware mode follows the target floating environment and does not promise identical subnormal, NaN or rounding behavior across all devices. The balanced reduction order and separate multiply/add operations remain unchanged; -O2 does not enable fast math.
